1) SPI Enable

sudo raspi-config
tab opens :
select interface option -> Spi enable
reboot :: sudo reboot or click raspberry icon -> shutdown -> reboot

2) Update your Pi:

sudo apt update
sudo apt upgrade

3) Install Python libraries:

sudo apt update
sudo apt install python3-venv python3-pip

4) Create a virtual environment

python3 -m venv rfid-env
source rfid-env/bin/activate

you should see: 
          (rfid-env) pi@raspberrypi:~

5) create a python file

nano rfid_read.py
Press CTRL + x → Enter (save)

6) Python code

from mfrc522 import SimpleMFRC522
import RPi.GPIO as GPIO

reader = SimpleMFRC522()

try:
    print("Place your RFID tag near the reader...")
    id, text = reader.read()
    print("ID:", id)
    print("Text:", text)

finally:
    GPIO.cleanup()

7) Run program

python rfid_read.py

Terminal shows:

Place your RFID tag near the reader...

Place RFID card near reader

UID and text appear

8) exit virtual environment

dectivate
